<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?><ns2:section xmlns:ns2="http://rest.cis.illinois.edu" id="57490" href="schedule/2016/spring/CHEM/590/57490.xml"><parents><calendarYear id="2016" href="schedule/2016.xml">2016</calendarYear><term id="120161" href="schedule/2016/spring.xml">Spring 2016</term><subject id="CHEM" href="schedule/2016/spring/CHEM.xml">Chemistry</subject><course id="590" href="schedule/2016/spring/CHEM/590.xml">Special Topics in Chemistry</course></parents><sectionNumber>F  </sectionNumber><creditHours>1 hours</creditHours><statusCode>A</statusCode><sectionText>1 Credit hour   PREPARING FUTURE FACULTY.        This course will teach essential skills to obtaining and succeeding in an independent academic career.  Topics will include: deciding whether academics is right for you, mechanics of a job search and interview skills, writing successful independent research proposals, setting up a research program and managing a group, teaching your first class, and getting tenure.  Different types of academic careers will be examined and an effort will be made to demystify the academy.</sectionText><sectionNotes>Restricted to Graduate - Urbana-Champaign.</sectionNotes><partOfTerm>1</partOfTerm><sectionStatusCode>A</sectionStatusCode><enrollmentStatus>UNKNOWN</enrollmentStatus><startDate>2016-01-19Z</startDate><endDate>2016-05-04Z</endDate><specialApproval>Departmental Approval Required</specialApproval><meetings><meeting id="0"><type code="LCD">Lecture-Discussion</type><start>02:00 PM</start><end>03:20 PM</end><daysOfTheWeek>M      </daysOfTheWeek><roomNumber>163</roomNumber><buildingName>Noyes Laboratory</buildingName><instructors><instructor lastName="Zimmerman" firstName="S">Zimmerman, S</instructor></instructors></meeting></meetings></ns2:section>